  "reason": "The records provide several relevant clues: rapid cooling affects phase formation in the closely related AlCoCrFeNiTi system (R16); composition and heat treatment can tune multiphase HEA structures (R1, R3, R5, R12, R17, R19); and magnetic-element substitution or phase constitution can reduce saturation magnetization while increasing coercivity (especially R1). Other records connect magnetism with fcc/hexagonal polymorphism or describe matrix–Laves microstructures. However, none discloses rapidly quenched FeCoNiTi with coexisting ferromagnetic fcc and C14 Laves phases, the compositionally matched C14-dominant control, Ti-sublattice antiferromagnetic coupling, or orbital/spin-canted domain-wall pinning. Thus the literature points toward processing- and phase-controlled magnetic behavior but leaves the specific intervention and mechanism requiring a substantial new idea."
